# wfg-log 1
# fixture plugins - the show's plugin set edited while a show runs (Phase 9a, PR 9a.4).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a session in which an entry was declared in the set with its
# four words and an identifier of its own, renamed, taken out and the delete undone
# reproduces exactly - the set made on demand under Audio at its fixed place, and
# every identifier on the record. Recorded from a real `wfg serve` of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/fx driven over OSC with no audio device; the header lines
# below are the session's own.
#
# bundle fx sha256:decba7b2295be26cf827b57037eabfb9afe0e4c01dc152cf822ff7546a198b07
# clock sampleRate=48000 blockSize=128 samplesPerTick=960
# media tone.wav 0 0.000
#
# DECLARED WITH ITS FOUR WORDS AND ITS OWN IDENTIFIER: name, the scan's identifier,
# the format, the path. A replay on a machine that has never scanned needs no
# known list to make the same entry - every word is on the record.
A 1 0 udp:127.0.0.1:60465 plugin.create s:"Verb" s:"VST3-0badf00d-verb" s:"VST3" s:"C:/plugins/verb.vst3" s:"PG7N0002"
#
# THE ONE ROW A HAND EDITS, renamed - an ordinary node.set on a persist=show row.
A 13 1 udp:127.0.0.1:60465 node.set s:"/godot/plugin/PG7N0002/name" s:"Hall"
#
# TAKEN OUT, AND THE DELETE UNDONE: the entry comes back whole, name and all, and the
# container that was made for the first entry stays.
A 26 2 udp:127.0.0.1:60465 object.delete s:"PG7N0002"
A 39 3 udp:127.0.0.1:60465 undo s:"document" s:"object.delete"
